# Design system conventions

- Check `src/components/ui/` (shadcn primitives) before writing custom markup for something
  standard (buttons, dialogs, dropdowns, form fields). Add a missing primitive via the shadcn CLI
  rather than hand-rolling it.
- Use Tailwind's design tokens / CSS variables (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.), not
  inline hex colors — this is what makes dark mode work for free.
- Icons: `lucide-react` exclusively, for consistency.
- Every interactive element must be keyboard-accessible. Base UI primitives (which shadcn wraps in
  this project) handle most of this already — don't bypass them with raw `<div onClick>`.
- shadcn/ui components here are built on Base UI, not Radix — polymorphism uses the `render` prop
  (e.g. `buttonVariants()` applied directly to a `<Link>`), not an `asChild` prop.
- Build with dark mode in mind from the start (use theme tokens), even before a toggle exists in
  the UI.
- Keep the palette neutral/zinc per the current design direction — don't introduce a new accent
  color without checking with the product owner first.

```tsx
// BAD
<div style={{ color: '#71717a' }} onClick={submit}>Submit</div>

// GOOD
<Button variant="secondary" onClick={submit}>Submit</Button>
```
